1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,220
A quality lead has an ingredient
lot in front of them.

2
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:09,800
The next question is practical:

3
00:00:11,020 --> 00:00:15,140
which production batches used it,
and where did those products go?

4
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:18,939
RecallScope brings that
path into one workspace,

5
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:22,360
with the original records
beside every connection.

6
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:26,820
This walkthrough uses the
supplied bakery sample records.

7
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:33,739
Here, one flour lot connects to four
production batches and four customer

8
00:00:33,740 --> 00:00:37,720
destinations, covering fourteen
hundred and forty delivered packs.

9
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:41,820
Select a batch, and its
route comes into focus.

10
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:45,520
Select a destination to see
the matching deliveries.

11
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:50,700
These totals are calculated from the
recorded relationships and quantities,

12
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:55,340
giving the operator a consistent
starting point for a recall drill.

13
00:00:56,433 --> 00:00:59,193
Let’s open the production
record behind this batch.

14
00:01:00,273 --> 00:01:04,293
The source identifies the flour
lot, twenty four kilograms used,

15
00:01:04,853 --> 00:01:06,493
and four hundred packs produced.

16
00:01:07,493 --> 00:01:11,772
The delivery register connects three
hundred and sixty of those packs to

17
00:01:11,773 --> 00:01:12,913
Orchard Pantry.

18
00:01:13,693 --> 00:01:17,812
The map is useful because each step
leads back to readable evidence,

19
00:01:17,813 --> 00:01:20,733
keeping the detail close to the decision.

20
00:01:21,833 --> 00:01:26,573
The document library holds all seven
source documents in this workspace:

21
00:01:27,973 --> 00:01:28,973
the supplier invoice,

22
00:01:29,573 --> 00:01:32,213
production sheets, and delivery register.

23
00:01:33,113 --> 00:01:37,832
Search a batch code to reach the relevant
record, or narrow the library by

24
00:01:37,833 --> 00:01:38,833
category.

25
00:01:39,173 --> 00:01:41,513
Workspace search also brings lots,

26
00:01:42,333 --> 00:01:43,333
batches,

27
00:01:43,453 --> 00:01:45,933
destinations, and document text together,

28
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:50,853
so the operator can move directly from
a question to its supporting record.

29
00:01:51,833 --> 00:01:53,633
Next, create a report.

30
00:01:54,553 --> 00:01:59,653
RecallScope saves the selected lot’s
delivery scope as a fixed snapshot,

31
00:02:00,413 --> 00:02:01,533
including the batches,

32
00:02:02,553 --> 00:02:03,512
destinations,

33
00:02:03,513 --> 00:02:05,773
quantities, and source references.

34
00:02:06,773 --> 00:02:11,392
Open it in the report reader to see
the same fourteen hundred and forty

35
00:02:11,393 --> 00:02:12,393
packs.

36
00:02:13,033 --> 00:02:17,852
The report remains available after a
reload, and reports for the same lot

37
00:02:17,853 --> 00:02:20,633
can be compared as the workspace changes.

38
00:02:21,667 --> 00:02:24,467
The interface is designed
for repeated use.

39
00:02:25,447 --> 00:02:26,647
Switch to night mode,

40
00:02:27,747 --> 00:02:33,026
choose comfortable or compact spacing,
and give the workspace a familiar

41
00:02:33,027 --> 00:02:34,027
name.

42
00:02:34,867 --> 00:02:37,367
These preferences stay on the device.

43
00:02:38,907 --> 00:02:43,807
Clear navigation and coordinated
selection keep the trace,

44
00:02:44,427 --> 00:02:49,906
documents, and reports within reach,
while the underlying records retain

45
00:02:49,907 --> 00:02:50,987
their identity.

46
00:02:52,067 --> 00:02:56,687
New documents enter through CSV
import or AI assisted reading.

47
00:02:57,667 --> 00:03:02,707
Fireworks is the configured provider,
with OpenAI support also available.

48
00:03:03,207 --> 00:03:06,527
AI proposes structured
fields from the source.

49
00:03:07,407 --> 00:03:12,146
The operator approves those records,
and deterministic code calculates the

50
00:03:12,147 --> 00:03:13,147
trace.

51
00:03:13,587 --> 00:03:17,646
This separation puts AI where it
helps with document interpretation,

52
00:03:17,647 --> 00:03:21,786
while keeping recorded quantities
and relationships inspectable.

53
00:03:21,787 --> 00:03:26,886
Original uploaded documents remain
accessible alongside the extracted

54
00:03:26,887 --> 00:03:27,887
information.

55
00:03:28,633 --> 00:03:33,372
The build follows the competition’s
AI first approach across all seven

56
00:03:33,373 --> 00:03:34,373
activities:

57
00:03:35,153 --> 00:03:36,173
idea generation,

58
00:03:36,833 --> 00:03:37,913
market research,

59
00:03:38,353 --> 00:03:41,633
user experience design, coding, testing,

60
00:03:42,073 --> 00:03:43,073
deployment,

61
00:03:43,253 --> 00:03:44,253
and pitch creation.

62
00:03:45,513 --> 00:03:47,733
The repository documents
those contributions,

63
00:03:48,613 --> 00:03:50,153
published source research,

64
00:03:50,733 --> 00:03:51,733
automated checks,

65
00:03:52,333 --> 00:03:54,213
and observed extraction runs.

66
00:03:55,133 --> 00:03:59,932
Judges can explore the live application,
inspect the implementation,

67
00:03:59,933 --> 00:04:03,293
and follow the decisions
behind the product.

68
00:04:04,333 --> 00:04:10,092
The first customer focus is a small
food producer whose quality lead

69
00:04:10,093 --> 00:04:15,073
manages supplier, production,
and dispatch records.

70
00:04:15,873 --> 00:04:21,132
The product brings those records into
an ingredient to customer workflow,

71
00:04:21,133 --> 00:04:25,273
with a proposed subscription
model for each site.

72
00:04:26,013 --> 00:04:29,213
RecallScope makes that workflow tangible:

73
00:04:30,573 --> 00:04:31,573
follow the lot,

74
00:04:32,193 --> 00:04:35,393
inspect the evidence, and keep the report.
